> Hi! I have RPi4, supervised HA in docker I have 3 BT devices (LYWSD03MMC, LYWSDCGQ, LYWSD02). On 22.8 all was Ok, on 22.9 nothing is Ok [bt.log](https://github.com/home-assistant/core/files/9565358/bt.log)

@participant7, i have sort of the same setup, RPI4, with raspbian, docker installed, with the HA docker container. 

Bluetooth is crashing after a while with message `tsocket.btmgmt_socket.BluetoothSocketError: Unable to open PF_BLUETOOTH socket` in the log. Is this something you also see? I try to use build in bluetooth adapter. How did you configure your docker container? Volumes, devices etc? Do you run container in privieged mode?
